PegResponsiveExponentialIrm::setIrmConfig(PegResponsiveExponentialIrmConfig)
├── given caller is not the current owner
│   └── it should reject before validation or checkpointing, including pending owners
└── given caller is the current owner
    ├── given configuration is invalid
    │   ├── when stressPrice is zero or not below recoveryPrice, or recoveryPrice exceeds the limit
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveExponentialIrmInvalidPriceConfig
    │   ├── when baseRate is zero, baseRate exceeds stressRate, stressRate reaches maxRate, or maxRate exceeds the limit
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveExponentialIrmInvalidRateConfig
    │   ├── when doublingDistance, recoveryDelay, or maxOracleAge is zero
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveExponentialIrmInvalidControllerConfig
    │   └── it should prioritize price then rate then controller errors before any checkpoint
    └── given configuration is valid
        ├── it should accept exact supported boundaries and adjacent valid values
        ├── it should not enforce a relationship between recoveryDelay and maxOracleAge
        ├── given market is unbound
        │   └── it should skip market queries and accrual
        ├── given market is paused
        │   └── it should query the exact PAUSE_TYPE and skip accrual
        ├── given market is active
        │   ├── it should accrue exactly once under the old inputs
        │   └── it should roll back all effects if the pause query or market accounting fails
        ├── it should store every new field and emit SetIrmConfig
        ├── it should reset prior recovery confirmation
        ├── when the observation is valid
        │   ├── it should apply the new curve and thresholds immediately
        │   ├── it should preserve stress hysteresis
        │   └── a healthy stressed observation should start a new recovery timer
        ├── when the observation is invalid
        │   ├── it should hold the rate within the new applicable floor and cap
        │   ├── it should preserve stress and clear recovery
        │   └── it should apply the same bounds while active, paused, or unbound
        ├── when the old stored or checkpointed rate exceeds the new cap
        │   └── it should accept and refresh within the new cap
        ├── when inputs equal the stored configuration
        │   └── it should still checkpoint and refresh
        ├── it should preserve the accrual timestamp when paused or unbound
        └── it should emit BorrowRateUpdated and IRStateUpdated after the setter and stress events
